      '#panel-explore': '<span class="sm-label sm-tag">Exploration · low density</span><p class="sm-display">The landscape is the star.</p><div class="sm-metric"><b>2.8%</b><span>of the screen with HUD.<br>State target: keep at least 90% clear.</span></div><ol class="sm-list"><li>Mission heading in the corner, at 55% opacity.</li><li>Prompt anchored to the evidence, showing the button of the controller in use.</li></ol><p class="sm-small"><b>Designed for</b> moments with no hostiles nearby; in the prototype, shortcut 1. Health, shield, ammo, radar and reticle leave the screen and stop taking keyboard focus.</p>',
      '#panel-combat': '<span class="sm-label sm-tag">Combat · tactical focus</span><p class="sm-display">Information follows the threat.</p><div class="sm-metric"><b>9.7%</b><span>of the screen with HUD.<br>Panels ease in over 450 ms, with fade and slide.</span></div><ol class="sm-list"><li>Dynamic reticle: the ring opens with recoil and closes in about 0.2 s.</li><li>Threat arc that rotates around the reticle toward the enemy.</li><li>Marker pinned to the target, projected from 3D every frame.</li><li>Shield in four segments and health in a separate bar.</li><li>Three-digit ammo, overheat, and reload and wheel prompts.</li><li>Orbital radar.</li></ol><p class="sm-small"><b>Comes in when</b> the player fires (or with shortcut 2). The center of the screen stays reserved for the reticle and the target.</p>',
      '#panel-critical': '<span class="sm-label sm-tag">Critical · peripheral alert</span><p class="sm-display">Urgency takes the edges.</p><div class="sm-metric"><b>12.0%</b><span>of the screen with HUD.<br>The alert grows at the edges; the reticle stays sharp.</span></div><ol class="sm-list"><li>Red vignette pulsing every 1.05 s.</li><li>Chromatic distortion that grows from the center to the edges.</li><li>Integrity alert with the recovery shortcut.</li><li>Panels turn red, with heartbeat and the word "critical".</li><li>Ammo turns red at six charges or fewer.</li></ol><p class="sm-small"><b>Designed for</b> health below 15%; in the prototype, shortcut 3. Color is never the only signal: every alert has text. With "reduce motion", the vignette holds still.</p>',
